# Sattva AI – User Acquisition Strategy

## 1. Objectives
- Define target user groups (e.g., wellness seekers, B2B clients, enterprises).
- Set measurable acquisition goals (e.g., X sign-ups, Y downloads, Z% retention).

## 2. Target Audience
- Personas: demographics, needs, motivations.

## 3. Channels & Tactics
- Organic: content marketing (blogs, wellness tips, SEO).
- Partnerships: tie-ups with wellness communities, employers, insurers.
- Paid: targeted ads on social platforms, newsletters.
- Product-led: in-app referrals, freemium models, trial offers.

## 4. Messaging Strategy
- Key value props: holistic wellness, AI-driven personalization, preventive care.
- Social proof: testimonials, success stories.

## 5. Acquisition Funnel
- Awareness → Interest → Sign-up → Activation → Retention.

## 6. Metrics & Goals
- KPIs: traffic sources, sign-up rate, activation, churn, customer acquisition cost (CAC), and lifetime value (LTV).

## 7. Testing & Optimization
- A/B tests on messaging, landing pages, onboarding flow.
- Feedback loops: surveys, usage analytics.

## 8. Timeline & Roles
- Phased milestones (e.g., Month 1: content setup; Month 2: partnerships; Month 3: growth campaigns).
- Who handles what.

## 9. Budget & Resource Allocation
- Estimate spend: digital ads, platform costs, content creation, team hours.

## 10. Reflection & Iteration
- Review performance weekly/monthly.
- Pivot or double down based on results.
